    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW26HKpAWZDaiUHoQ6yyQQEt8)_\n\n## What\n\n`tools/quick-capture-native` no longer waits for Emacs. It now:\n\n1. asks for the line in the macOS dialog (or takes it as an argument, skipping the dialog),\n2. writes it atomically to a spool folder (`~/.local/state/quick-capture`, override with `QUICK_CAPTURE_SPOOL`),\n3. pokes Emacs in the background with `emacsclient -n -e '(sp-quick-capture-drain)'` and returns.\n\n`sp-quick-capture-drain` (new) files the queued lines oldest first and deletes each file. It runs on the poke, 2 seconds after the module loads (lines captured while Emacs was down), and after `sp-quick-capture-drain-interval` (30) idle seconds. Failures go to `failed/` in the spool. The file's mtime is the capture time, used for `:CREATED:` and for relative dates (`!tom`), so a line filed days later still means what you meant.\n\n## Why this approach\n\nBefore, `emacsclient -e` blocked while Emacs was busy and the line was lost when Emacs was not running. A spool file keeps the task safe on disk and needs no extra tool: AppleScript and bash are already used, and Hammerspoon, Shortcuts, Alfred or Raycast can call the script (with an argument, if they have their own input box). Writing straight into `inbox.org` from bash was rejected: it would race with the open Emacs buffer and duplicate the parser.\n\n## Tests\n\n- 4 new ERT tests (capture time, ordering, partial files ignored, failures parked, no spool); all 13 pass in Emacs 29.3 batch.\n- Real daemon on Linux: with the daemon stopped (`SIGSTOP`) the script returns in 0.02 s and the line is filed on resume. Plain `emacsclient -n` did hang for 15 s on a stopped daemon, which is why the poke runs in the background. With the daemon dead the line stays queued.\n- Not run on macOS (dialog, notifications, hotkey launchers).\n\nThe module is tangled from `docs/tangles/text/sp-quick-capture.org`; CHANGELOG entry is in the Quick capture set.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi8rzNjcERW7a7X5wyd)_",
